{"decision": "repair", "edits": [{"start_line": 75, "end_line": 105, "replacement": "always @* begin
    i = 0; 
    frame_len_next = frame_len_reg;
    frame_len_valid_next = 1'b0;
    frame_next = frame_reg;

    if (monitor_axis_tready && monitor_axis_tvalid) begin
        if (!frame_reg) begin
            frame_len_next = 0;
            frame_next = 1'b1;
        end

        if (KEEP_ENABLE) begin
            bit_cnt = 0;
            for (i = 0; i <= KEEP_WIDTH; i = i + 1) begin
                if (monitor_axis_tkeep == ({KEEP_WIDTH{1'b1}}) >> (KEEP_WIDTH-i)) bit_cnt = i;
            end
            frame_len_next = frame_len_next + bit_cnt;
        end else begin
            frame_len_next = frame_len_next + 1;
        end

        if (monitor_axis_tlast) begin
            frame_len_valid_next = 1'b1;
            frame_next = 1'b0;
        end
    end
end
"}], "explanation": "The original combinational logic fails to reset the frame length accumulator for single-word frames (where tlast is asserted while frame_reg is 0). The reset only occurs in the `else if (!frame_reg)` branch, which is skipped when tlast is true. The fix restructures the logic to always reset the accumulator when starting a new frame (frame_reg=0 and tready&&tvalid), then add the byte count, and finally handle tlast to mark frame valid and clear frame_reg."}
